**Verdict:** trust **strained**, value **high**, delight **clear_hit** — recommendation **revise**. The portrait is fundamentally fair: his agency stays in his failures, the harshest claim (installed discipline) is carried by people he credits himself, and the psychological center is his own on-record sentence.

**Blockers:** 1 (plus 7 concerns). **SUBJECT-R1:** the "Why Travis Kelce Wears No. 87" section states the origin story as settled fact, but Jason Kelce publicly dismissed it on New Heights in Nov 2025 as "the biggest load of bull****" — "You have somehow retroactively worked this in" (confirmed this review via [Yahoo Sports](https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/jason-kelce-dismisses-travis-kelce-070641727.html), [The SportsRush](https://thesportsrush.com/nfl-news-its-the-biggest-load-of-sht-jason-kelce-shoots-down-travis-kelces-emotional-jersey-number-story/), [The Mirror](https://www.themirror.com/sport/american-football/travis-kelce-jersey-number-chiefs-954527), [Reality Tea](https://www.realitytea.com/2025/11/25/jason-kelce-on-travis-chiefs-jersey-number-story/)). The proposed repair upgrades the thesis: a Seven retroactively converting an arbitrary number into a monument to his brother is *stronger* Type 7 evidence than the tidy origin story.

**Strongest hit:** the Super Bowl shove section — offense at full strength, Jason's rebuke, Kelce's unhedged "It's definitely unacceptable," Reid's grace, then the overtime win; criticism explained without being erased.

